{
  "title": "Fix Vscode Extension Uri Resolution and Navigation",
  "status": "open",
  "prompt": "The semio repo vscode extension should properly resolve all URIs and navigate to them. Clicking on a URI should navigate to the resource, clicking on a tree item should navigate to the resource, the `semio-repo: Navigate to` command should navigate to the resource.",
  "summary": "Fixed bundle tree items showing raw kind strings (e.g. 'librarysemio/js') instead of emoji-prefixed short names (e.g. '📚js'). Added bundleKindEmoji() mapping function matching the Go CLI's bundleKindEmoji() (schema→🛂, binary→⌨️, ui→🖱️, site→🌐, assets→🏪, library→📚). Fixed label to extract short name after '/' from full bundle name. Also removed leftover duplicate constructor/refresh in FilterTreeDataProvider. Added bundleKindEmoji tests.",
  "github": {
    "issue": "https://github.com/usalu/semio/issues/441"
  },
  "goal": "AI-OPTIMIZED-REPO/REPO-CLIENT/REPO-VSCODE-EXTENSION",
